course: dictionary
lesson: 9819
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Sweep is a good example: it can be a doing word (a verb) or a naming word (a noun).
explain: «Mice sweep their whiskers back and forth many times a second to feel the shape of things around them.» Mice are not cleaning anything here. Sweep means to move in a long, smooth, curving way.
explain: «Broken glass is swept up carefully with a brush and dustpan.» Sweep up means to clean up. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then check that your meaning still makes sense.
fact: Sweep can be a verb, like «sweep the floor», or a noun, like «one long sweep of the arm».
fact: «Sweep» means to clean with a brush or broom, pushing dirt away.
fact: «Sweep» means to move quickly and with force over an area, as in «The wave swept the sandcastle away».
fact: «Sweep» means to move in a long, smooth, curving way, as in «She swept her arm across the table».
fact: A chimney sweep is a person who cleans chimneys, and in history many chimney sweeps were children doing a hard and dangerous job.
exercise: «Mice sweep their whiskers back and forth many times a second.» What does sweep mean here? | To shout loudly | To swim fast under water | To clean a floor with a broom | *To move in a long, smooth, curving way
exercise: «The wave swept the sandcastle away.» What does swept mean? | To sleep softly | *To move quickly and with force over an area | To build slowly | To clean with a brush
exercise: Dad says, «Please sweep the kitchen floor.» What does sweep mean? | To paint the walls | To cook a meal | *To clean with a brush or broom | To swim fast
test: «Broken glass is swept up carefully with a brush and dustpan.» What does sweep up mean here? | Drop the glass on the floor | *Clean up dirt and pieces with a brush | Pick up the glass with bare hands | Make a loud noise
test: In «She made one long sweep of her arm across the table», what kind of word is sweep? | A verb, a doing word | *A noun, a naming word | An adjective, a describing word | A question word
exam: «As the Earth spins, morning sweeps round the planet.» What does sweeps mean here? | To break into small pieces | *To move in a long, smooth, curving way | To clean the planet with a brush | To stop suddenly
